chosen:
Since $\angle AEF$ and $\angle EFG$ are alternate interior angles, they are equal. Hence  \begin{align*}
\angle EFG &= \angle AEF \\
&= 1.5x.
\end{align*} Moreover, since $\angle AEF$ and $\angle EFC$ are alternate interior angles, they must be equal, so we have \begin{align*}
2x + \angle EFC &= 1.5x \\
\angle EFC &= -0.5x
\end{align*} Since $\angle FCB$, $\angle EFC$, and $\angle EFG$ are supplementary, we have   \begin{align*}
\angle FCB + \angle EFC + \angle EFG &= 180 \\
x + (-0.5x) + 1.5x &= 180 \\
x &= \boxed{60}.
\end{align*}
</think> <answer>60</answer>

